WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.947
- It has never been

00:00:01.947 --> 00:00:04.859
more beneficial to be a good person

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:06.200
than it is right now,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.886
because the shadows of our society

00:00:07.886 --> 00:00:09.078
are being exposed

00:00:09.078 --> 00:00:11.157
by the distribution of communication.

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:13.824
(hip hop music)

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.709
What am I doing right now?

00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:21.649
Is she here?

00:00:21.649 --> 00:00:22.482
I want to stay on track,

00:00:22.482 --> 00:00:23.315
I got a lot going on.

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:24.648
What's up, Vlog?

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:27.098
What's up W.T. Clark High School

00:00:27.098 --> 00:00:29.586
big shout out to Samir.

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:32.074
Hope you're representing
Vayner proper, my man.

00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:35.402
Two seconds for all the
high school kids, listen.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:38.226
You're young, and that's your
strength and your weakness.

00:00:38.226 --> 00:00:39.059
Right?

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:40.586
First and foremost, the weakness.

00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:42.307
Like, you haven't accomplished shit.

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:43.642
I don't know, you better beep that.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:44.660
'Cause I'm sure they're
not gonna let it play

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.034
in a high school, but,

00:00:46.034 --> 00:00:47.058
edit it, beep it.

00:00:47.058 --> 00:00:48.590
You haven't accomplished shit!

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.530
And you've got the audacity like you have.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.076
On the flip side that's your strength,

00:00:53.076 --> 00:00:53.962
you're young.

00:00:53.962 --> 00:00:55.394
And you've got your whole
life in front of you.

00:00:55.394 --> 00:00:57.380
And all of you are trying
to prove yourselves,

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.100
put yourself on, have stuff.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.514
And that's gonna make you impatient.

00:01:01.514 --> 00:01:03.594
Please recognize how young you are,

00:01:03.594 --> 00:01:05.570
and get real, real, real patient.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.860
And last of all, find that thing,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.901
whether it's eSports and video games

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.226
whether it's basketball,

00:01:11.226 --> 00:01:12.875
whether it's painting or writing,

00:01:12.875 --> 00:01:15.186
people are gonna tell
you it's not practical.

00:01:15.186 --> 00:01:16.494
But it is.

00:01:16.494 --> 00:01:17.938
Find your passion and go deep,

00:01:17.938 --> 00:01:19.538
put in 18 hours of work.

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:20.914
Don't lay on the couch and go through your

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:22.002
Instagram feed.

00:01:22.002 --> 00:01:24.118
Put in the work, find your passion,

00:01:24.118 --> 00:01:26.698
know that you're young,
which means you're impatient,

00:01:26.698 --> 00:01:29.252
but you've got nothing but time.

00:01:29.252 --> 00:01:31.210
(reflective music)

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:32.538
- [Female] What advice
do you have for women

00:01:32.538 --> 00:01:34.210
who just kind of carry around that baggage

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.444
that they can't make it
as a female entrepreneur?

00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:38.370
- You know, I think
that's a great question.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.811
I think there's a couple things
that run through my mind.

00:01:39.811 --> 00:01:40.882
Number one,

00:01:40.882 --> 00:01:44.266
I love that the internet
has eliminated the

00:01:44.266 --> 00:01:46.214
truth behind a man's world.

00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:47.442
You know, now,

00:01:47.442 --> 00:01:50.026
I'm not naive and I don't
want to come across tone-deaf.

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:52.450
I am the first and have been for

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.962
long before it was popular,

00:01:53.962 --> 00:01:55.650
like it sure seems now,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.050
like everybody's different.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.026
There are clearly advantages
for being a white male

00:01:59.026 --> 00:02:00.025
in America,

00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:01.850
versus a female, versus a minority,

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.946
versus being born in Iran,

00:02:03.946 --> 00:02:05.671
that's just real life.

00:02:05.671 --> 00:02:06.939
I think the bigger part,

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:09.201
and I was an early investor in Birchbox

00:02:09.201 --> 00:02:10.995
and Micmac and brit.co

00:02:10.995 --> 00:02:11.828
and

00:02:12.673 --> 00:02:13.576
I've, to be very frank

00:02:13.576 --> 00:02:14.805
have done quite well with my

00:02:14.805 --> 00:02:16.253
female entrepreneurial ventures

00:02:16.253 --> 00:02:18.861
because they have been underpriced in cost

00:02:18.861 --> 00:02:21.671
because it has been a
'man's world' in VC Land.

00:02:21.671 --> 00:02:24.141
And there has been a disrespect
of the female entrepreneur.

00:02:24.141 --> 00:02:27.374
And I'm not Mother Teresa
or this amazing human being,

00:02:27.374 --> 00:02:28.957
I'm just a businessman and I'm like,

00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:31.501
it would never cross my mind to think that

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.261
a woman or an alien or a Latino

00:02:34.261 --> 00:02:36.189
couldn't do it as well.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.229
And so,

00:02:37.229 --> 00:02:39.485
in a weird way I think
I took advantage of the

00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:42.161
shortcomings of a lot of white males

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.951
and it was mainly on
the back of knowing that

00:02:43.951 --> 00:02:45.957
the internet doesn't
give a shit who you are.

00:02:45.957 --> 00:02:47.781
My thesis that I wrote in Crush It,

00:02:47.781 --> 00:02:49.302
and The Thank You Economy

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.949
has played out, which is,

00:02:50.949 --> 00:02:52.278
the internet doesn't care.

00:02:52.278 --> 00:02:54.021
Everybody's got a shot.

00:02:54.021 --> 00:02:57.063
You're more than welcome
to go on Twitter and CNN

00:02:57.063 --> 00:02:59.936
and dwell from 7pm to 11pm

00:02:59.936 --> 00:03:02.948
and shit on everybody, and call people out

00:03:02.948 --> 00:03:06.482
and be upset and say this
one's bad and this one's good.

00:03:06.482 --> 00:03:08.961
How about instead of those
four hours dwelling in the muck

00:03:08.961 --> 00:03:12.255
of all this, realizing that
what it means is this is the

00:03:12.255 --> 00:03:15.199
greatest opportunity ever
for anybody and everybody.

00:03:15.199 --> 00:03:16.639
Because as long as you have this

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:18.343
and I get emails from
people that are homeless

00:03:18.343 --> 00:03:19.880
every single day of my life,

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.009
who have this.

00:03:21.009 --> 00:03:22.848
This is an unlock.

00:03:22.848 --> 00:03:25.135
We need perspective.

00:03:25.135 --> 00:03:26.687
Like everybody's on
their fuckin' high horse

00:03:26.687 --> 00:03:27.895
and judging.

00:03:27.895 --> 00:03:30.608
For every entrepreneur
that's listening right now,

00:03:30.608 --> 00:03:32.431
go on the offense!

00:03:32.431 --> 00:03:33.991
What do I say?

00:03:33.991 --> 00:03:37.343
Make that woman chip on
your shoulder get real big

00:03:37.343 --> 00:03:39.943
and use it as a driver of positivity

00:03:39.943 --> 00:03:42.831
and opportunity, not looking backwards.

00:03:42.831 --> 00:03:44.159
Whatever you are,

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:45.623
being the best version of what you are is

00:03:45.623 --> 00:03:47.336
always going to be the right strategy and

00:03:47.336 --> 00:03:50.113
I think we need to talk
more about self awareness.

00:03:50.113 --> 00:03:52.369
The secret sauce is don't
overcomplicate stuff.

00:03:52.369 --> 00:03:53.831
You have to work hard

00:03:53.831 --> 00:03:55.527
you have to work smart,
you have to be empathetic

00:03:55.527 --> 00:03:58.375
and grateful, you have to
be positive and optimistic

00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.017
and every time you're not,

00:04:01.017 --> 00:04:03.063
you're giving points off the board.

00:04:03.063 --> 00:04:04.280
You don't have to be optimistic,

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.617
maybe you were born pessimistic.

00:04:05.617 --> 00:04:09.233
But please understand that
will detrimentally hurt you

00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:10.900
in your ambitions of

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.576
if you want to be an entrepreneur

00:04:13.576 --> 00:04:15.480
because it takes blind optimism,

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.856
because everything in
your face every day is

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.976
telling you no.

00:04:17.976 --> 00:04:21.152
And you're completely,
completely committed to yes.

00:04:21.152 --> 00:04:22.272
- [Ray Dalio] Hello, Gary!

00:04:22.272 --> 00:04:23.402
- It's good to see you, Ray.

00:04:23.402 --> 00:04:24.408
