(laughs)

00:04:25.477 --> 00:04:27.128
- The tide is turning.

00:04:27.128 --> 00:04:28.523
- I'm in control.

00:04:28.523 --> 00:04:29.432
- I'm worried about this!

00:04:29.432 --> 00:04:30.515
- I know!

00:04:30.515 --> 00:04:31.904
- This is real energy coming from you.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:32.936
- Okay!
- I'm excited.

00:04:32.936 --> 00:04:34.200
- Okay and I'm in control.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.033
Gary!

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:35.866
- Yes, sir.

00:04:35.866 --> 00:04:36.920
- Okay, we're gonna do this.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.184
I'm gonna do it to you, man.

00:04:38.184 --> 00:04:39.017
- I'm listening.

00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:39.850
- Okay.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.683
So

00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:41.516
what I'm trying to do is to

00:04:41.516 --> 00:04:42.516
help you all

00:04:43.892 --> 00:04:46.658
understand what the best
principles of winners are.

00:04:46.658 --> 00:04:49.954
They're winning because
they're doing things.

00:04:49.954 --> 00:04:52.421
They're operating by recipes, essentially.

00:04:52.421 --> 00:04:54.239
They're doing those things over and over

00:04:54.239 --> 00:04:55.653
that makes them winners.

00:04:55.653 --> 00:04:57.933
Okay so Gary is a winner.

00:04:57.933 --> 00:04:59.773
And now we're gonna get into

00:04:59.773 --> 00:05:01.287
Gary's principles.

00:05:01.287 --> 00:05:02.120
- [Gary] Here we go.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.032
- Here we go!

00:05:03.032 --> 00:05:04.356
What do you think you're going after

00:05:04.356 --> 00:05:06.533
and where did it come from?

00:05:06.533 --> 00:05:08.050
- My intuition on this

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.047
and I do think I spend a lot of time on it

00:05:10.047 --> 00:05:10.887
is,

00:05:10.887 --> 00:05:13.727
I feel like I'm going after

00:05:13.727 --> 00:05:15.060
all-time legacy.

00:05:17.647 --> 00:05:20.564
I think that it comes from a mix of

00:05:22.528 --> 00:05:26.028
guilt, gratitude, insecurity and optimism.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.247
Because I was such a poor
student at such a young age

00:05:31.247 --> 00:05:32.090
- [Ray] Me too.

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.287
- And because I wasn't a good athlete,

00:05:34.287 --> 00:05:35.402
in any shape or form,

00:05:35.402 --> 00:05:38.951
it eliminated the two things
that boys were judged on

00:05:38.951 --> 00:05:39.839
when I grew up.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.711
Either you were a good
student and going to Harvard,

00:05:41.711 --> 00:05:44.679
or you were a tremendous
athlete and going to USC.

00:05:44.679 --> 00:05:46.376
I was neither.

00:05:46.376 --> 00:05:48.159
Entrepreneurship was surely not cool

00:05:48.159 --> 00:05:49.826
in 1984, 5, 6 and 7.

00:05:51.143 --> 00:05:52.744
So what I was doing off the field

00:05:52.744 --> 00:05:53.791
or out of school

00:05:53.791 --> 00:05:55.177
was making money,

00:05:55.177 --> 00:05:57.671
but that wasn't deemed as a merit

00:05:57.671 --> 00:05:58.975
or a remarkable act.

00:05:58.975 --> 00:06:00.159
- I hear you.

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.543
And so that void of the intellectual

00:06:03.543 --> 00:06:04.708
is then also what

00:06:04.708 --> 00:06:06.168
you're demonstrating.
- 100 percent.

00:06:06.168 --> 00:06:07.001
- Great!

00:06:07.001 --> 00:06:09.880
- I am completely driven
by a chip on my shoulder.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.297
On my upbringing,

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:15.327
except that I am empathetic
to everybody else

00:06:15.327 --> 00:06:17.687
so it's not manifesting as a negative.

00:06:17.687 --> 00:06:19.120
It's manifesting as a positive.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:20.511
- Boy, you're doing a good job, man.

00:06:20.511 --> 00:06:22.184
Okay, this is going good.

00:06:22.184 --> 00:06:25.235
Tell me about those principles
that you think would be

00:06:25.235 --> 00:06:26.561
helpful, that have helped you.

00:06:26.561 --> 00:06:27.728
- No question.

00:06:29.329 --> 00:06:31.089
I am an unbelievable buyer,

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:34.756
and I think the grossly
underestimated trait

00:06:36.424 --> 00:06:38.424
in the capitalistic game

00:06:39.435 --> 00:06:40.585
is empathy.

00:06:40.585 --> 00:06:42.321
Empathy will give you leverage

00:06:42.321 --> 00:06:43.451
with the other party.

00:06:43.451 --> 00:06:44.284
- Boom!

00:06:44.284 --> 00:06:45.169
There's a principle!

00:06:45.169 --> 00:06:46.313
- But because of empathy

00:06:46.313 --> 00:06:48.633
and it is my binary north star,

00:06:48.633 --> 00:06:52.992
I temper my expectations
of others on my team

00:06:52.992 --> 00:06:55.492
and try to be realistic
to their realities.

00:06:55.492 --> 00:06:58.304
Watching others with a lot of freedom

00:06:58.304 --> 00:07:00.352
gives me context of how to put them in the

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:02.107
best position to succeed.

00:07:02.107 --> 00:07:04.452
- Insecurity will lead

00:07:04.452 --> 00:07:06.285
to undermining actions

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.773
that hurt the merit of your organization.

00:07:09.773 --> 00:07:13.211
I am dumbfounded by people
positioning themselves

00:07:13.211 --> 00:07:16.772
and their businesses
as if life is a sprint

00:07:16.772 --> 00:07:18.747
when it is clearly a marathon.

00:07:18.747 --> 00:07:20.484
I am devastated

00:07:20.484 --> 00:07:22.733
that people make short
term financial decisions

00:07:22.733 --> 00:07:25.539
to buy something that
closes the short term gap

00:07:25.539 --> 00:07:26.857
in their insecurity,

00:07:26.857 --> 00:07:28.275
and at the undermining of

00:07:28.275 --> 00:07:29.810
their long-term wealth and happiness.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.643
- Okay.

00:07:30.643 --> 00:07:34.492
- Having humility to carry
two opposing points of view

00:07:34.492 --> 00:07:35.814
and making them rub up against each other

00:07:35.814 --> 00:07:36.829
- Okay, that's another one!

00:07:36.829 --> 00:07:37.662
(laughs)

00:07:37.662 --> 00:07:38.495
So let's,

00:07:38.495 --> 00:07:39.545
we're gonna split that, okay?

00:07:39.545 --> 00:07:41.027
- I've got principle for days, kids!

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:41.860
- Okay.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.693
- You know,
- Okay

00:07:42.693 --> 00:07:44.092
- Having the humility to be able to

00:07:44.092 --> 00:07:44.972
- Have humility

00:07:44.972 --> 00:07:48.476
- Have humility in being
able to carry opposing views

00:07:48.476 --> 00:07:51.213
on an issue, and then creating friction

00:07:51.213 --> 00:07:53.757
and making a judgment in
the context of the moment.

00:07:53.757 --> 00:07:54.590
- Failure.

00:07:55.444 --> 00:07:56.777
- Is tremendous.

00:07:58.621 --> 00:08:00.508
I'm wearing a New York
Jets Christmas sweater,

00:08:00.508 --> 00:08:02.998
not a New York Yankees Christmas sweater.

00:08:02.998 --> 00:08:06.446
And at six years old, I
passionately cared about both.

00:08:06.446 --> 00:08:08.996
There's deep insight into my love affair

00:08:08.996 --> 00:08:10.487
with the Jets and the Knicks.

00:08:10.487 --> 00:08:11.320
They have

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.232
- Tell me in the failure

00:08:12.232 --> 00:08:13.231
how, follow that through,

00:08:13.231 --> 00:08:14.064
what you do like

00:08:14.064 --> 00:08:15.055
about failure?
- I prefer

00:08:15.055 --> 00:08:17.391
I prefer the journey over the riches.

00:08:17.391 --> 00:08:21.169
My personal wealth is disproportionately

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:23.649
being sabotaged by myself

00:08:23.649 --> 00:08:26.880
because I enjoy the
process of gathering it.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.844
I literally think I

00:08:27.844 --> 00:08:29.286
- That's smart.

00:08:29.286 --> 00:08:30.973
It's smart because you're not

00:08:30.973 --> 00:08:32.749
you're out, look.

00:08:32.749 --> 00:08:34.597
What you're doing is you're realizing

00:08:34.597 --> 00:08:37.103
what really has value.

00:08:37.103 --> 00:08:38.115
Okay?
- You're right.

00:08:38.115 --> 00:08:40.472
- Money, one of the challenges of money is

00:08:40.472 --> 00:08:42.415
it's easy to count.

00:08:42.415 --> 00:08:43.871
And because it's easy to count,

00:08:43.871 --> 00:08:45.431
then people sort of say, I count it up

00:08:45.431 --> 00:08:46.503
but I got more of that

00:08:46.503 --> 00:08:47.929
and that's the thing of success.

00:08:47.929 --> 00:08:50.983
If you can have happiness points,

00:08:50.983 --> 00:08:52.271
if you can count happiness

00:08:52.271 --> 00:08:53.104
- [Gary] I'm winning

00:08:53.104 --> 00:08:54.591
- We would optimize for happiness

00:08:54.591 --> 00:08:58.568
so what you're doing is
optimizing for happiness,

00:08:58.568 --> 00:09:00.258
you're not optimizing for money.

00:09:00.258 --> 00:09:01.639
That's a lot smarter.

00:09:01.639 --> 00:09:03.210
- There's so much more upside on both

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.521
legacy and wealth

00:09:04.521 --> 00:09:06.647
when you make it about legacy.

00:09:06.647 --> 00:09:08.816
Especially compounded in,

00:09:08.816 --> 00:09:10.639
what people do very poorly,

00:09:10.639 --> 00:09:11.472
here is a principle.

00:09:11.472 --> 00:09:14.847
People are very bad at understanding

00:09:14.847 --> 00:09:16.991
the new context of communication

00:09:16.991 --> 00:09:19.095
and they're deploying old principles

00:09:19.095 --> 00:09:20.400
on new playing fields.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.495
It has never been

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:24.087
more beneficial

00:09:24.087 --> 00:09:26.695
to be a good person than it is right now,

00:09:26.695 --> 00:09:28.703
because the shadows of
our society are being

00:09:28.703 --> 00:09:31.970
exposed by the distribution
of communication.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.751
Owning your shortcomings

00:09:33.751 --> 00:09:36.679
and bringing awareness to them

00:09:36.679 --> 00:09:39.399
is disproportionate strength and leverage

00:09:39.399 --> 00:09:40.327
in the long term.

00:09:40.327 --> 00:09:41.160
- Boom!

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.820
- Which is exposing your own shortcomings,

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.580
morally, intellectually,

